  "name": "Golpe larense (golpe tocuyano)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The golpe is the secular festive dance-song of Lara state, especially El Tocuyo and Barquisimeto, played by golpero groups on cuatro, the five-string cinco, maracas and a stick-beaten tambora drum, with high lead singing answered by the group, and danced by couples at parties and festivals. Pío Alvarado and Los Golperos de Don Pío are its best-known recorded exponents. The cuatro card covers the cuatro and cinco and the membrane-drum card stands in for the tambora.",
